{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack","id":638589,"title":"A vampire in the pack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-24T18:34:19-07:00","id":638589,"title":"A vampire in the pack","content":"So we are starting a game of Werewolf 2nd edition and one of our players wants to play a vampire. The GM has tentatively okayed it and we are not trying to consider all the complications that come along with a vampire member of a pack.<br /> <br /> Anyone done this yet? Any tips that would help make this a fun experience for all involved? We have a blessed pack and a vampire that is a close, close friend with the pack alpha.<br /> <br /> For the record, she will not be playing a gangrel. She'll probably be playing Daeva, Ventrue or Mekhet, and will be unaligned as far as covenants.<br /> <br /> Primary concerns are balance, the fact that the player is out of any daytime pack activity, the fact that a large portion of the game takes place in the Shadow (can vampires even enter the shadow except through a verge?). Is group pathfinding a thing still in 2e and if so would the vampire lose all their clothes? In general how would a vampire fit in with a pack of werewolves socially speaking? Would they necessarily be on a rung below the werewolves as far as hierarchy? Would they get totem bonuses? (I know that's a no).<br /> <br /> Just wondering what the general opinion and advice on this sort of thing is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T20:18:27-07:00","id":638726,"title":"","content":"1- I did;<br /> <br /> 2- If the ST don't want to mix vampire's politics, there are no need for it. If she want to do, there are no harm in it, either. Both work well.<br /> <br /> 3- Balance is a given of sorts. The vampire will be good at her stuff, but no worries about anyone there being overshadowed.<br /> <br /> 4- Daytime activity have two possibilities. If it is frequent and the game primarily about werewolf stuff, just give the vampire an item to get rid of sunburns. If infrequent, just work through it.<br /> <br /> 5- Vampires can enter the Shadow as much as any human can. The werewolves can find ways to do so, specially in 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> 6- I think things are easier now.<br /> <br /> 7- Socially each pack is a unique thing. That means that its fit depends entirely on the group, no hard rules.<br /> <br /> 8- The same as above, hierarchy doesn't even need to be a thing in the pack. Or the vampire can have a high standing if the pack decides so. In my game the Alpha was a wolf-blooded and the Beta was his mortal wife. They got things done, so the pack didn't complained.<br /> <br /> 9- I don't remember any rule that forbid vampires from getting the same treatment as mortals, so yes, they can. They can get all the pack benefits, and actually invest on the pack's Totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T23:32:06-07:00","id":638850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=638726#post638726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9- I don't remember any rule that forbid vampires from getting the same treatment as mortals, so yes, they can. They can get all the pack benefits, and actually invest on the pack's Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans get the totem's advantage, but they don't have the Totem merit and don't contribute towards the totem. (Supporting-cast Wolf-Blooded are limited to a single dot in the Totem merit as well p.91.)Unless your Storyteller decides otherwise, a Vampire pack member does gain the totem advantage, but can't contribute to the Totem merit - she lacks the connection to the <i>Hisil</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T23:46:12-07:00","id":638853,"title":"","content":"Yep, this is why they had a Bloodline in Requiem 1e that specifically could buy the Totem Merit and join a pack. Second Edition would likely just make it into a Merit for ease of use. And then you have the Ordo Dracul Coil that would just let you straight up buy Wolf-Blooded Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T01:49:44-07:00","id":638875,"title":"","content":"If entering the shadow is something the vampire wants to be better at, there's the blood tenebreous discipline from the book of spirits.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that wolfblooded that get transformed into another supernatural creature (other than werewolf) can retain their tell(s), while a tell to say let the vampire daywalk would be inappropriate, a tell to deal better with spirits or the hisil would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T11:25:47-07:00","id":639325,"title":"","content":"Last month my players and I played a similar game too. One of my players wanted to play a vampire in our pack. He had the same intentions. However this vampire was going to have a difficult time in keeping up with our pack. So we decided to make him a Gangrel in the dead wolves bloodline and circle of the crone. With Sublunario it made it easier for him in our pack, with all the benefits. As for spirit dealing, he use cruac that deals with spirits (from CotC covenant book). <br /> <br /> We also made a couple of devotions cause he wanted his character to know all the werewolf forms too. Wolf form was easy already, protean 3. Human form given (of course). Near human protean 2 &amp; 4. As for the other two...<br /> <br /> Shape of the Beast's Wrath (war form)<br /> <br /> Protean 4 and Sublunario 4 <br /> <br /> Savage Hound (near wolf)<br /> <br /> Protean 3 and Sublunario 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T12:59:05-07:00","id":639389,"title":"","content":"Why would you allow him to play a vampire if you're gonna give him all the Uratha forms? Did that include the Gauru healing factor, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T14:25:18-07:00","id":639466,"title":"","content":"Special Snowflake <i><b>gotta be </b></i>Special... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T15:44:28-07:00","id":639534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=639389#post639389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you allow him to play a vampire if you're gonna give him all the Uratha forms? Did that include the Gauru healing factor, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>He wanted his character to learn the other forms, so why not. It went nicely in our game. As for the form mechanics, no we follow vampire mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T18:28:10-07:00","id":639676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=638850#post638850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans get the totem's advantage, but they don't have the Totem merit and don't contribute towards the totem. (Supporting-cast Wolf-Blooded are limited to a single dot in the Totem merit as well p.91.)Unless your Storyteller decides otherwise, a Vampire pack member does gain the totem advantage, but can't contribute to the Totem merit - she lacks the connection to the <i>Hisil</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation was that the humans didn't got the Merit just for ease of the rules for pack creation. The same reason for the Wolf-Blooded to only begin with one dot: not because they can't have more, but because those where NPC's creation rules for a pack.<br /> <br /> Anyway, some limitations only have to be in place if the ST wan't, they're not a balance issue. The weakness to fire is a balancing issue for vampires, it gives them a weakness ready to be used by an enemy with thorough preparation, as is silver to Uratha. But the weakness to sun light is just a thematic enforcer. If the ST want to use this theme, it stays. But if not, she doesn't have to even give a cost for ways to get rid of it. A magical ring or extra-super-special spiritual blessing is more than enough explanation for this vampire to walk in the daylight with the pack. Or simply ignore that the weakness ever existed.<br /> <br /> The same goes for any obstacle in dealing with werewolf's themes. You can even give the vampire a Devotion to cross the Gauntlet free of cost, simply because this ability isn't powerful in your game, but instead simply default.<br /> <br /> Just take care to not give for free anything that REALLY makes the game easier compared to the Uratha. Alternate forms isn't a bad idea if the player wants it, but it certainly should cost. Only get rid of limitations that don't play on balance in THIS chronicle and would only get in your way. Difficulties to do some common things, if still doable to the degree needed, should stay in place to also reinforce the theme of the difference between the splats (a natural theme in most crossovers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T20:12:35-07:00","id":639774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=639676#post639676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, some limitations only have to be in place if the ST wan't, they're not a balance issue. The weakness to fire is a balancing issue for vampires, it gives them a weakness ready to be used by an enemy with thorough preparation, as is silver to Uratha. But the weakness to sun light is just a thematic enforcer. If the ST want to use this theme, it stays. But if not, she doesn't have to even give a cost for ways to get rid of it. A magical ring or extra-super-special spiritual blessing is more than enough explanation for this vampire to walk in the daylight with the pack. Or simply ignore that the weakness ever existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you just stay at BP of 2 and then the sunlight damage is negligible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T23:48:27-07:00","id":639894,"title":"","content":"You can just rule that sunlight doesn't affect her in the Shadow, then focus large segments of your story on nighttime or in the Shadow. You shouldn't have to change major game mechanics to make the game playable if you want to avoid the mess. As for clan I would go with Daeva, that way your vampire fills a slot that most wolves never will unless they make it their character's focus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T01:33:02-07:00","id":639965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=639894#post639894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can just rule that sunlight doesn't affect her in the Shadow, then focus large segments of your story on nighttime or in the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it is somehow official, as Sun is said to be under the clouds most of the time in <i>Hisil</i>. and Luna to favor other beings of the night, contrasted to her/his sibling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T03:22:54-07:00","id":640026,"title":"","content":"Since Helios is specifically noted to be harsh and unchanging, forcing everything away with the pressure of his radiance, and not in his nature to forgive or relent, it's unlikely he'd give vampires a pass just because they're in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> He's still pissed at werewolves, he probably wouldn't be nicer to a vampire who was allied to the subjects of his ire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T03:42:45-07:00","id":640034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=640026#post640026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Helios is specifically noted to be harsh and unchanging, forcing everything away with the pressure of his radiance, and not in his nature to forgive or relent, it's unlikely he'd give vampires a pass just because they're in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> He's still pissed at werewolves, he probably wouldn't be nicer to a vampire who was allied to the subjects of his ire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called 'the Shadow' for a reason, tho. There's even precedent in the first edition Book of Spirits about how dimmed sunlight is in it compared to vampiric banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T03:59:21-07:00","id":640043,"title":"","content":"And 2nd edition specifically points out that Helios is the source of pressure pushing everything out of the Shadow, he gives it gravity through this pressure, he stills and settles Essence. Yes, it's called the Shadow for a reason, and if I was running the OP's game I might be inclined to step back the relative strength of the damaging light, but I'd still make it damaging.<br /> <br /> As always, people can change and play how they want. I encourage everyone to do so. I like these discussions to raise what these groups may want to consider, because changes rarely happen in isolation, and I want people to enjoy the changes they make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:06:17-07:00","id":640198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=640043#post640043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And 2nd edition specifically points out that Helios is the source of pressure pushing everything out of the Shadow, he gives it gravity through this pressure, he stills and settles Essence. Yes, it's called the Shadow for a reason, and if I was running the OP's game I might be inclined to step back the relative strength of the damaging light, but I'd still make it damaging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically? That's not how Gravity works.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T09:43:00-07:00","id":640364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=640198#post640198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically? That's not how Gravity works.</div> </div> </div> </div>and just like that i have another thing for the &quot;next time someone calls me condescending/patronizing/passive-aggressive&quot; file<br /> <br /> The sidebar in Second Edition that contextualizes this discussion has the word bracketed in quotation marks and the fact that we're talking about a realm of symbolism where predation manifests in every way from the literal to the hyper-figurative means this observation is <i>extra</i> useless. Helios is the reason for the Shadow phenomenon loosely analogous to gravity and how the actual force works in reality has no bearing on the fact that the nigh-omnipresent god-being-slash-law-of-physics is still less likely to be negotiated around a defining weakness of a crossover splat by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T21:26:20-07:00","id":641058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=639894#post639894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can just rule that sunlight doesn't affect her in the Shadow, then focus large segments of your story on nighttime or in the Shadow. You shouldn't have to change major game mechanics to make the game playable if you want to avoid the mess. As for clan I would go with Daeva, that way your vampire fills a slot that most wolves never will unless they make it their character's focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't a mess because it isn't a major game mechanic. From a strictly mechanic standpoint damage from sunlight have almost no effect on the game, and almost no other rule reference it. The sole exceptions are the effects of Humanity and Blood Potency on said damage, but given how common it is expected in a vampire game for this to be an issue, I'd say those traits will hardly be thrown from balance because sunlight damage is gone.<br /> <br /> Again, it is a major theme in Vampire, and should be considered with caution. But really, the game doesn't suffer any mechanical setback for sunlight damage's removal, and the chronicle isn't about vampires to begin with. It can still be interesting to let the sun hurt the vampire, but it is pretty easy to get rid of this if it gets in the way of the actual themes of he chronicle.<br /> <br /> Remember that nothing here is about the official setting, about Requiem, or about other games. Its about this guy's chronicle.<br /> <br /> The other issues I think simply aren't issues in 2nd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T22:37:56-07:00","id":641149,"title":"","content":"If you really don't want to change the rules regarding sunlight then it would be easy enough to just place most of the action at night. Unless you have placed your game in a rural setting (possible with wolves) then the streets probably don't role up after dark, stores are still open, parties taking place and certainly most crimes and acts of violence take place after dark. For those times when it simply has to be done during the day? I recommend limiting them as much as you can and keep them as short as you can so the vampire player doesn't feel left out too much of the time. If they really want to play a vampire then dealing with the splat's weaknesses should be part of the challenge, not a deal breaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T23:09:49-07:00","id":641179,"title":"","content":"I mostly agree, then comes the last line.<br /> <br /> The point: depending on the chronicle, it isn't a challenge, its just boring.<br /> <br /> But again, I mostly agree. I would make the most to keep the weakness unless it really starts to keep in the way of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Sorry to be shooting this again and again, but I really hate when someone tries to say that there is a <u>right</u> way to play a game. It is a game. Weakness isn't important. Fun is important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T23:25:13-07:00","id":641192,"title":"","content":"I know I'm in the minority on this but to me the only interesting part of vampires is the weaknesses and how do you overcome them. I'm too old to enjoy playing fourteen year old fantasies of being the meanest and badest mofo in the room, or bagging the hottest girl with my wicked wiles, I want to overcome obstacles big and small. In my first requiem chronicle (I'm currently running the second) my players nearly lost all my willingness to run it when I threw a simple sunlight challenge at them, totally prepared to go very easy on any solutions they came up with, and the response I got was a &quot;that won't be a problem&quot;, followed by making it clear they really didn't want to worry about it. That's the reason we have ended up playing more werewolf and mage than vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T00:38:26-07:00","id":641260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641179#post641179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to be shooting this again and again, but I really hate when someone tries to say that there is a <u>right</u> way to play a game. It is a game. Weakness isn't important. Fun is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone has said there's a right way. That said, I personally find special snowflake players increase boredom in games. You want to play a vampire in our werewolf game? *sigh* Okay, let's see how we can make it work. You want to play a vampire but not have to worry about any vampire inconveniences? Why play a vampire at all? <br /> <br /> If it's about fun, and you can't have fun by playing a werewolf in our werewolf game, either you're not going to have fun in this game, or the allowances everyone else has to make for your special snowflake drops everyone else's fun.<br /> <br /> That's been my experience, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T01:34:09-07:00","id":641283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641260#post641260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think anyone has said there's a right way. That said, I personally find special snowflake players increase boredom in games. You want to play a vampire in our werewolf game? *sigh* Okay, let's see how we can make it work. You want to play a vampire but not have to worry about any vampire inconveniences? Why play a vampire at all?<br /> <br /> If it's about fun, and you can't have fun by playing a werewolf in our werewolf game, either you're not going to have fun in this game, or the allowances everyone else has to make for your special snowflake drops everyone else's fun</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not player just play as Ordo Drcaul character? They have Coils for crossovers as one of reasons in Covenant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T02:22:34-07:00","id":641292,"title":"","content":"They can play as whatever they want. I was saying that in my experience, when a group gets together to play X, and one person just has to play Y for whatever reason, the concessions required to accommodate Y means X's fun suffers.<br /> <br /> As I said before, I don't believe anyone here has said that there's a right way to play. The OP said the group was trying to consider all the complications a vampire in a werewolf pack would bring. We've not even scratched the surface, but ultimately, which aspects impact play will be decided by the group. The spectrum runs from playing a vampire by the (Requiem) book and taking on board all the vampire condition and society crap that comes with that, to playing something with Forsaken rules that the group calls a vampire but has none of the actual nWoD connotations or baggage, and requires work from the ST to decide how the not-werewolf uses werewolf rules to demonstrate its specific condition. How many complications (the OP's word) come into that depends where on the spectrum the group wants the vampire to occupy.<br /> <br /> As a sidenote, few things about nWoD vampires pisses werewolves off faster than Ordo Dracul and their parasitic drive to drain Wyrm's Nests (read: loci), so good luck with that. (Caveat - I'm assuming OD still like doing this in 2nd edition. I've not delved as deeply into the Ordo's 2nd ed drives.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T04:38:26-07:00","id":641393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641292#post641292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a sidenote, few things about nWoD vampires pisses werewolves off faster than Ordo Dracul and their parasitic drive to drain Wyrm's Nests</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is ironic, considering the Coil of the Ascendant is probably your best bet to get a vamp that can work in a chronicle that has frequent daylight scenes. <br /> <br /> Still, the main thrust now is <i>studying</i> stuff. So you could have a Dragon who decided to try learning about nests by consulting the resident experts on the subject and kinda went from there to somehow end up getting inducted into the pack. And now they're considered the local &quot;dragon nest guy&quot; or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T05:33:05-07:00","id":641414,"title":"","content":"I like vampires as stay-up-all-night people, and also die-burning-and-screaming-in-the-sun people.<br /> <br /> I've had vampires close to packs before but not in second edition. I suppose if I was going with second edition and let a player play a vampire in a werewolf game I'd suggest the players build a totem that required them to perform the sacred hunt, or hunt in general, at night. That way while the vampire might not be able to participate in everything, they'd at least be part of the core werewolf experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T06:17:04-07:00","id":641443,"title":"","content":"I had a similar thing in a game, a player wanted to play a dead wolf but the bloodline is horrible system wise. So i simply use Ahrimanes bloodline from masquerade with a few twitches with the disciplines. Spiritus for the garou form, ogham for the spirit side and fortitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641149#post641149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really don't want to change the rules regarding sunlight then it would be easy enough to just place most of the action at night. Unless you have placed your game in a rural setting (possible with wolves) then the streets probably don't role up after dark, stores are still open, parties taking place and certainly most crimes and acts of violence take place after dark. For those times when it simply has to be done during the day? I recommend limiting them as much as you can and keep them as short as you can so the vampire player doesn't feel left out too much of the time. If they really want to play a vampire then dealing with the splat's weaknesses should be part of the challenge, not a deal breaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt it backward on the shadow? I remember reading, i could be wrong, that if you cross to the shadow at night its day and vice versa.<br /> <br /> As for the sunlight in the shadow you could play as the vampire having to stick to the &quot;shadow spots&quot; when travelling there or just forget about the weakness only in the shadow. Just my 2 cents there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-27-2015, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T06:18:56-07:00","id":641444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641414#post641414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like vampires as stay-up-all-night people, and also die-burning-and-screaming-in-the-sun people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at low potency, high humanity the best you can get is slowly cooking.<br /> <br /> Seriously the frailest vampire possible with no blood in them would take an hour and 40 minutes to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 08-27-2015, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T06:33:39-07:00","id":641450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641444#post641444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, at low potency, high humanity the best you can get is slowly cooking.<br /> <br /> Seriously the frailest vampire possible with no blood in them would take an hour and 40 minutes to die.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if they're wearing heavy clothes and sunglasses, they don't burn at all. Though they're still taking the -1 to everything from not getting a good day's sleep and anything strenuous will probably make those clothes fall off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T06:37:06-07:00","id":641453,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the responses so far. I doubt we'll be getting rid of the vampire's sunlight weakness, though that might be an-in game goal of ours. It's more likely that the pack will work around the daytime until then. She also will be necessarily Circle of the Crone (for in game reasons, as the game is an extension of our last game), so no Ordo Dracul shortcuts unfortunately.<br /> <br /> That said, our game is already a crossover in the sense that there is heavy werewolf, vampire and mage presence in the city, with many overlapping 'territories'. So the inclusion of the vampire character might add a layer of complication to our dealings with them, or might just make things easier.<br /> <br /> Lastly I'll add that I don't think our player is the special snowflake type. It's just that when we were voting on what game to play, we had 4 people who wanted werewolf and 1 who wanted vampire because she just likes vampires more, and so we just figured hey, why not give everyone what they want. Otherwise she probably would not have been as excited to roleplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T07:07:37-07:00","id":641482,"title":"","content":"So let she be concerned to be Low on Blood Potency and High Humanity. End effect would like <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mick St. John</span></span></span> from <b>Moonlight </b>series. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=odR0IUH3c38\" data-code=\"odR0IUH3c38\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/odR0IUH3c38/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T07:22:26-07:00","id":641503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641443#post641443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt it backward on the shadow? I remember reading, i could be wrong, that if you cross to the shadow at night its day and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it works normally. I suppose you could say activity levels tend to be the opposite, as Helios puts a lot of spirits to dormancy or across the Gauntlet during the day, while inhabitants seem more active at night. Not counting Helions, probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641444#post641444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, at low potency, high humanity the best you can get is slowly cooking.<br /> <br /> Seriously the frailest vampire possible with no blood in them would take an hour and 40 minutes to die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was expressing my preference, not a reflection of the mechanics. And slow damage is more of a decay. Their flesh rots and sloughs off their bones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-27-2015, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T11:45:01-07:00","id":641905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641453#post641453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all the responses so far. I doubt we'll be getting rid of the vampire's sunlight weakness, though that might be an-in game goal of ours. It's more likely that the pack will work around the daytime until then. She also will be necessarily Circle of the Crone (for in game reasons, as the game is an extension of our last game), so no Ordo Dracul shortcuts unfortunately.<br /> <br /> That said, our game is already a crossover in the sense that there is heavy werewolf, vampire and mage presence in the city, with many overlapping 'territories'. So the inclusion of the vampire character might add a layer of complication to our dealings with them, or might just make things easier.<br /> <br /> Lastly I'll add that I don't think our player is the special snowflake type. It's just that when we were voting on what game to play, we had 4 people who wanted werewolf and 1 who wanted vampire because she just likes vampires more, and so we just figured hey, why not give everyone what they want. Otherwise she probably would not have been as excited to roleplay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another option is letting the vampire character have a ghoul that tries to help her archieve her goals during day time. If you have a good player, you could just have him or her play the ghoul during the day, and vampire during the night (except in emergy situations of course, where the vampire might be woken).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T13:14:22-07:00","id":643304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=641192#post641192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm in the minority on this but to me the only interesting part of vampires is the weaknesses and how do you overcome them. I'm too old to enjoy playing fourteen year old fantasies of being the meanest and badest mofo in the room, or bagging the hottest girl with my wicked wiles, I want to overcome obstacles big and small. In my first requiem chronicle (I'm currently running the second) my players nearly lost all my willingness to run it when I threw a simple sunlight challenge at them, totally prepared to go very easy on any solutions they came up with, and the response I got was a &quot;that won't be a problem&quot;, followed by making it clear they really didn't want to worry about it. That's the reason we have ended up playing more werewolf and mage than vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you like to play the weaknesses of a vampire, that's perfectly ok. It does make for good games more often than not.<br /> <br /> But you're implying that NOT wanting to play them is to play a childish, immature game, and that older people shouldn't play such things. And to me it only says that you are both narrow focused (for not seeing other possibilities for drama) and arrogant (for judging maturity by the way people like to play a game).<br /> <br /> The OP is the only one who can say what's good for his group, and I presented an option among others.]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone has said there's a right way. That said, I personally find special snowflake players increase boredom in games. You want to play a vampire in our werewolf game? *sigh* Okay, let's see how we can make it work. You want to play a vampire but not have to worry about any vampire inconveniences? Why play a vampire at all? <br /> <br /> If it's about fun, and you can't have fun by playing a werewolf in our werewolf game, either you're not going to have fun in this game, or the allowances everyone else has to make for your special snowflake drops everyone else's fun.<br /> <br /> That's been my experience, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every PC is a special snowflake, to begin with. Every single one. It is the job of any sensible ST to assure this, even if the PC's backstory says she's a completely normal person. It only says that the character is even more special for achieving this state without being &quot;groomed by destiny&quot; for the role of a snowflake in the world.<br /> <br /> What disrupts most games is a player that wants to play something that disrupts the game. And that IS a valid concern. You're describing a situation where the player wants a character that blow up some core assumptions of the game the group wants to play just to be allowed. And yes, a lot of people who want to play a vampire in a werewolf game are going to disrupt things by forcing core assumptions of the game to be tuned down in the interest of the character. Someone who wants a character more special than the others.<br /> <br /> Not always the case, though, and that's my whole point. Sometimes the strange PC doesn't disrupt anything. That's what have to be analysed. What the group expect from the game, what the ST have in mind for the game, what effect is to be expected for this single chronicle. I already played and narrated games where a &quot;special snowflake&quot; almost ruined everything. And I played games where it worked. Only the OP can analyse the situation, what I can do is to suggest ways to make it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there are other ways to do what the OP want. I would probably use both <b>nofather</b> and <b>Penta</b>'s last suggestions, myself. To make the Totem favor night activity, and the player to have a Ghoul that can be played at daytime. A little tweak of the rules for the Pack is enough, you just put a Ghoul in the pack in the place of one of the Wolf-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T14:45:53-07:00","id":643427,"title":"","content":"Someone's taking it personal, apparently. Anyway. I agree with Bunyip. &quot;I wanna play a vampire, but can I get the werewolf forms plz?&quot; reeks of Marie-Sue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T23:24:59-07:00","id":643828,"title":"","content":"At the risk of offending someone else I will also state that I don't care for playing politics, romances or great tragedies. I like investigation, conflict and saving the day (GTA left me cold). Personally I see nothing \u200bwrong with splat crossovers or party imbalance, as long as everyone enjoys the game story can be adapted to cover all of the bases. I think the easiest answer would be to focus the chronicle on night time scenes, giving each members strengths and weaknesses a chance to shine. You already have to do this when dealing with both Rahu and Eldoth (?), so why not with wolves and vampires? Personally I find that easier if the player enjoys his character's limits as much as his strengths. If your player goes with the ghoul idea (which is probably the whole reason ghouls were included in the first place) I would strongly advise they make a ghoul character they like just as much as their vampire, not just a cheap extension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T23:42:26-07:00","id":643838,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> just a few thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. The sunlight issue<br /> In my opinion, you should'nt make this easy for the vampire. Sunlight is the primary ban for vampires, and it should always stay a problem. However, for low-blood potency high-humanity vampires, it is not that much of an issue. Additionally, the according frenzy trigger is that the vampire get hurt by sunlight, which a young vampire can avoid easily in many situations. Cruac should offer some tricks to make unlife at day easier in the future, especially with reagards to waking up and maybe enduring sunlight for a short amount of time on very high levels.<br /> <br /> Sun in Hisil does not have to be a problem in my opinion. It is the sun that burns the vampire, not some strange spiritual reflection of it. Certainly, from the viewpoint of the werewolves, Helios is the sun, but it should be the viewpoint of the vampire that counts here. Not sure if there are any rules, but I would let sunlight damage a vampire only in the &quot;real&quot; world.<br /> <br /> 2. Crossing the gauntlet<br /> Here are a few ideas:<br /> - Give a pack member or the pack totem the ability to transport the vampire to the other side<br /> - An artifact: There is an item that allows for crossing the gauntlet like a werewolf. But where does it come from? Maybe there are hidden costs?<br /> - The witch: A powerful member of the circle can grant our vampire the ability to cross the gauntlet for some time by means of a powerful spell (Yes, according to the book that isn't possible, but I never liked that rule. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). But what is her price? She surely has her own agenda and reasons...<br /> <br /> 3. Speaking to spirits<br /> You should grant her the ability to speak with spirits early on. If she knows Cruac, it could be possible with a low level spell to speak their language.<br /> <br /> 4. Werewolf forms<br /> I see no reason why a vampire should have the ability to shapeshift like a werewolf. In combat, a vampire can keep up with her fighting disciplines. Faster running and hightened senses can also be granted by disciplines and merits. In my opinion, a vampire should be a vampire and not an undead werewolf copy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T10:37:11-07:00","id":644401,"title":"","content":"On shapeshifting bats, I rather favored protean 5 from the bloodlines pc game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T11:13:12-07:00","id":644438,"title":"","content":"Whether or not sunlight harms vampires in the Shadow depends entirely on Helios' mood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T11:51:06-07:00","id":644457,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out that while it's not entirely clear how much of the 1e material translates, Book of Spirits made vampires in the Shadow not enter the daysleep and only take a point of bashing damage per turn from exposure to sunlight (which was already a significant downgrade from the bare minimum threat it could pose in the Flesh in 1e).<br /> <br /> For the sake of a comparative metric for any hypothetical conversions, replicating the minimum rate of damage from 1e (1 agg/turn) in 2e uses a vampire with Humanity 4 and Blood Potency 4-5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T12:16:16-07:00","id":644467,"title":"","content":"I do take it personal when someone seems to me to be arguing something in the line of &quot;this is the right way to play the game&quot;. As I said, it is a pet peeve of mine. A serious one. So I get easily carried over.<br /> <br /> And for the record, the thing about sunlight damage wasn't even to take out weaknesses, but a very practical problem the OP was concerned about. In a all-Vampire game it is a source of drama and nothing else. Everyone will still face the same problems and, overall, play together. In a Werewolf chronicle it could get in the way of the chronicle. The player in question never considered to get rid of the weakness, it is an option in case the weakness turns out boring in the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:16:47-07:00","id":644616,"title":"","content":"It's probably worth noting that the bane of vampires is sunlight, not just the sun. So providing you're not going to throw the spirit world out the window, Helions would have just as much impact on a vampire in the Hisil as Helios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T23:16:39-07:00","id":645040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=644616#post644616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably worth noting that the bane of vampires is sunlight, not just the sun. So providing you're not going to throw the spirit world out the window, Helions would have just as much impact on a vampire in the Hisil as Helios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that occurred to me on subject - if what is hurting vampires in material world is sunlight, and in 1ED sole existence of Helios in <i>Hisil</i> did not burn vampires - maybe it's because Helions <b>are</b> <i>Hisil</i> sunbeams? Think of it - in Spirit World EVERYTHING has spirit. So even Light of Moon and Sun have it's spirits. As there are five different &quot;lights&quot; and their &quot;inspirations&quot; we have five courts of Lunes - they send different &quot;lights&quot; of Luna to the world. With the same take Helions would be the proper Sun's Lights - so unless vampire meet one, they would be relativity safe in <i>Hisil</i>.<br /> <br /> But then confrontation with Helion would be almost instant Final Death for the undead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-30-2015, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T13:42:18-07:00","id":645851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/638589-a-vampire-in-the-pack?p=645040#post645040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that occurred to me on subject - if what is hurting vampires in material world is sunlight, and in 1ED sole existence of Helios in <i>Hisil</i> did not burn vampires - maybe it's because Helions <b>are</b> <i>Hisil</i> sunbeams?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they did burn vampires, just slower, and one bashing per turn isn't anything to sneeze at when you can't heal naturally. But not everything is an active spirit. Beams of sunlight can be Helions, but they can also be light from Helios, or sunlight essence filtering through the gauntlet or dormant sunlight spirits.<br /> <br /> You'd think meeting a living reflection of the sun <i>would</i> destroy vampires. I don't see why there's any issue with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-30-2015, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}